Ticket work (functional or purely technical) goes through **PILOT**, a lightweight
alternative to running the full BMAD-METHOD agent framework — five short phases
(`plan` → `investigate` → `lay out` → `operate` → `test & validate`), each its own
isolated, low-token agent context instead of one accumulating one. Its skills
(`.claude/skills/pilot-*`) and agent personas (`.claude/agents/pilot-*.md`) are copied
into this repo from the `pilot` distribution repo (github.com/Jonas-Eve/pilot) rather
than written here from scratch: the phase skills are invoked as `/pilot-story`,
`/pilot-scope`, `/pilot-spec`, `/pilot-dev`, `/pilot-review` — driven one phase at a
time, there's no single command that runs the whole pipeline end to end.
`docs/pilot-process.md` in this repo is a verbatim copy of that repo's canonical spec —
the state machine, labels, and claim protocol — kept in sync by `/pilot-update`, never
hand-edited here. Read it before creating or moving a ticket through any phase.
